{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795282684,"nonce":"GlDIbYd0+Vnrpx/MfCHt4Juc2x0=","title":"Several machines agree on one match through ordered messages","message":"**Outcome.** sim::wire defines the messages State, Hit, Kill, Launch, Burst, EndMatch, Lobby, and Profile. sim::Timeline shows a remote plane between two real states, with a delay that follows the jitter. One type holds the match of one machine: it steps the planes that the machine owns, and it applies the messages in the order of the bus. sim::lobby holds the rules of the lobby, and sim::room holds the text frames of the bus.\n\n**Requirements.** N4, N5, N6, L2, L6, L7.\n\n**Done when.** Tests of sim run several machines over an ordered bus in memory: every machine counts the same kills, a hit takes effect only on the machine that owns the target, the bots pass to the next host when the host leaves, and a remote plane never steps backward when states arrive in bunches.\n\nBelongs to the plan, issue 1d9449d.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}